From 6e60636a7ef2a2f700f80ca1eded2a6d9957c529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 16:57:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(legal): ship Terms of Service page so Meta + App Store
 reviewers have a real URL to point at
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a Legacy-Table-specific Terms of Service page at /terms covering:
acceptance, service description, eligibility (13+), account
responsibility, user-generated content rights + license, acceptable
use, App Store/Play Store subscription terms (auto-renew + cancel
instructions for iOS and Android), third-party services, IP, account
termination + deletion (linking to existing /delete-account route),
disclaimers, limitation of liability, privacy reference, governing
law (California), changes, and contact (support@legacytable.app).

Mirrors PrivacyPolicyPage's structure and styling so the two read as a
matched set. Renders in the same Navigation chrome when the user is
logged in; uses the public header + 'Back to Login' button otherwise.

Wires the footer 'Terms of Service' links in LandingPage.jsx and
landing/PricingPage.jsx from the previous disabled placeholder
(href='#', cursor-not-allowed) to a real <Link to=/terms>.

Unblocks:
- Meta for Developers Publish flow (Settings → Basic requires
  Privacy URL + Terms URL + Data Deletion URL).
- App Store Connect resubmissions for Legacy Table that need a real
  Terms URL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
